      "math_academy_id": "q-35246",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}},$ where ${c}_{1}=-2{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=-3{b}_{1}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5{b}_{1}-2{b}_{2} \\\\  & =-2{b}_{2}+5{b}_{1} \\\\  & =-2{b}_{2}-\\frac{5}{3}(-3{b}_{1}) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}-\\frac{5}{3}{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}].$",
